# Root line-ending policy.
#
# Why this file exists
# --------------------
# This repository records SHA-256 digests of exact file bytes and verifies them
# on every `npm run agent:validate` / `npm run agent:security` run:
#
#   agent-platform/tooling/graphify-requirements.txt            -> core-tooling.json's requirementsSha256
#   agent-platform/tooling/security-python-requirements-*.txt   -> security-tools.lock.json's requirements_sha256
#   plus the artifacts checked by scripts/check-high-risk-remediations.py
#   and scripts/build-agent-audit.py --check
#
# Every developer machine here has `core.autocrlf=true`, and until now the
# repository root had no .gitattributes — only platforms/{claude,codex,
# antigravity}/ had one. That meant a plain `git checkout`, `git switch`,
# `git pull`, `git restore`, or fresh clone would rewrite LF to CRLF on disk
# for every text file outside platforms/, silently invalidating those digests.
#
# This is not hypothetical. On 2026-08-07 a diagnostic `git stash`/`git stash
# pop` flipped AGENTS.md, core-tooling.json, and both tooling requirements
# files from LF to CRLF and broke three hash checks that had nothing to do with
# the work in progress. See .solo/risks.md and .solo/decisions.md (T24). The
# response at the time was "avoid git stash", which addressed one trigger and
# left checkout, pull, switch, restore, and clone unprotected.
#
# `eol=lf` makes checkouts byte-stable across Windows, macOS, and Linux, so the
# recorded digests mean the same thing on every machine. This mirrors the
# policy platforms/*/.gitattributes already applies to the distributions.
#
# Note: this changes what FUTURE checkouts write. It does not rewrite files
# already on disk. The index was already LF everywhere, so adding this produces
# no diff — it only stops the conversion from happening on the way out.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never pass through newline conversion. Auto-detection
# usually catches these, but the digests above make an incorrect guess
# expensive, so they are declared explicitly.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mp3 binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.wasm binary

# Detached signatures cover exact bytes; newline conversion would invalidate
# them (graphify-out/.graphify_labels.json.sig).
*.sig binary
